P1 — SECURITY HARDENING
=======================

================================================================
73. CROSS-TENANT FUZZ / PROPERTY TESTS
======================================

Generate random:

organizations
projects
jobs
IDs

Attempt cross-scope operations.

Invariant:

principal never obtains resource outside authorized scope.

Property-based testing is welcome.

================================================================
74. IDOR TESTS
==============

Guess valid identifiers belonging to another tenant.

Test:

API
CLI service layer
artifact download
realtime streams
audit
usage

No insecure direct-object-reference leak.

================================================================
75. SSRF HARDENING
==================

Enterprise-controlled URLs include possible:

OIDC discovery
SIEM endpoint
webhook
MCP
artifact callback

Protect:

localhost
link-local
metadata endpoints
private networks according to policy
redirect chains
DNS rebinding where relevant

Do not rely solely on string blacklist.

================================================================
76. SCIM SECURITY REVIEW
========================

Verify:

auth
tenant scope
pagination
filter bounds
payload size
deactivation
group mapping
rate limits

Do not claim full SCIM conformance without explicit conformance tests.

================================================================
77. API KEY HASHING
===================

Audit API key storage.

Never store plaintext.

Use suitable cryptographic hashing/MAC scheme for high-entropy API keys.

Test database dump does not reveal usable credentials.

================================================================
78. SESSION SECURITY
====================

Review:

browser cookies
CSRF
session expiry
role changes
membership removal

A user whose membership is removed must lose access within documented
cache/session bounds.

================================================================
79. AUTHORIZATION CACHE
=======================

If authorization decisions are cached:

tenant scope
policy version
principal
resource/action

must be represented correctly.

Policy/member changes require bounded invalidation.

================================================================
80. PLATFORM ADMIN ABUSE BOUNDARY
=================================

Platform admins are high privilege.

Audit all cross-tenant access.

Consider reason/ticket requirement for support access.

Do not pretend operational administrators cannot bypass controls if they
actually can.

================================================================
P1 — MULTI-REGION OPERATIONS
============================

================================================================
81. REGION HEALTH
=================

Expose:

AVAILABLE
DEGRADED
UNAVAILABLE

for:

workers
artifact storage
provider
control plane dependencies

================================================================
82. REGIONAL CIRCUIT BREAKER
============================

When a region becomes unhealthy:

stop scheduling new work there.

Do not immediately migrate stateful jobs without recovery analysis.

================================================================
83. RESIDENCY-AWARE FAILOVER
============================

Failover target must satisfy organization residency policy.

If no allowed target exists:

PAUSE / WAITING_CAPACITY

not:

violate residency.

================================================================
84. REGIONAL CAPACITY
=====================

Scheduler should understand:

capacity by region
runtime by region
queue depth
tenant restrictions

================================================================
85. COST AWARE ROUTING
======================

Optional routing may consider cost.

Security/residency constraints always override cheapest-region logic.

================================================================
86. LATENCY TEST
================

Inject network latency between worker and PostgreSQL.

Measure:

claim latency
lease renewal
heartbeat
outbox

Report environment and results.

================================================================
87. NETWORK PARTITION TEST
==========================

Use deterministic failure injection.

Worker loses DB connectivity while running.

Verify:

no new external mutation after lease authority is lost according to
configured safety window.

================================================================
88. STALE-WORKER EXTERNAL SIDE EFFECT TEST
==========================================

Fencing protects DB writes but cannot magically stop GitHub API calls.

Ensure external mutation path validates current ownership immediately
before high-risk side effects where practical.

This is critical.

================================================================
89. OUTBOX OWNERSHIP
====================

External side effects should preferably originate from durable outbox
processing under current authoritative state.

Avoid arbitrary worker direct external mutations where transactional
reconciliation is needed.

================================================================
90. DUPLICATE PR/MERGE UNDER PARTITION
======================================

Simulate timeout after GitHub accepted:

create PR
merge

Reconcile before retry.

No duplicate PR / double merge request.

================================================================
P2 — HA ARCHITECTURE PROOF
==========================

================================================================
91. POSTGRESQL HA BOUNDARY
==========================

If ZCoder relies on external managed PostgreSQL HA:

document contract:

endpoint behavior
failover expectations
connection retry
RPO/RTO assumptions

Do not implement a half-baked DB clustering system inside ZCoder.

================================================================
92. FAILOVER HARNESS
====================

Create an integration interface to test endpoint interruption/failover.

Use a reproducible local setup if practical.

Do not claim managed-cloud HA without actual cloud test.

================================================================
93. API HORIZONTAL SCALE
========================

Run multiple API processes against one PostgreSQL.

Test:

auth
job submission
idempotency
realtime
webhook ingestion

No sticky in-memory security state.

================================================================
94. RECONCILER MULTI-INSTANCE
=============================

Run more than one reconciler instance.

Ensure leader election/idempotency prevents duplicate effects.

================================================================
95. SCHEDULER MULTI-INSTANCE
============================

Prove multi-scheduler safety.

Do not depend on singleton deployment unless architecture explicitly
requires it and readiness enforces that assumption.

================================================================
96. REGIONAL CONTROL-PLANE LIMIT
================================

If control plane remains one region:

say:

multi-region workers supported
multi-region control plane NOT implemented

Do not blur the distinction.

